The SD card tile, over t715-sdcard

The microSD slot's own tile, after the Modem one: on while the card is mounted,
off with a card in but not mounted (a tap mounts it, about a second) or with no
card. The session's udiskie already mounts a card that goes in, so the tile
shows and changes the state rather than owning it. A long press opens the card
in Files (Disks when it cannot be read). Without the command or the slot no
sdcard key is probed and the tile stays dimmed, so an image without t715-sdcard
or a kernel without the slot never fails. Against omarchy-mobile 87b8395
(omamobile-shell 0.2.94) and the patches before it, packages/omamobile-shell.

